### Career context

**Checked first-person biography.** Stone's site describes joining Apple in 1986, working in multimedia and later on special projects for John Sculley, joining Microsoft Research in 1993, co-founding and directing the Virtual Worlds/Social Computing group, teaching at NYU's ITP, becoming a Microsoft vice president in 2000 and leaving Microsoft in 2002. These are attributed biographical statements. [Stone, “About”](https://lindastone.net/about/).

This account does not establish individual inventorship of every contemporary Apple or Microsoft product. The original's categorical claims about product ownership, compensation, absence of appointments and comparative career success are removed. Career history also supplies no causal connection to the user's AI sessions.

### Concepts

| Concept | Corrected description | Evidence type |
|---|---|---|
| Continuous partial attention | Stone's account of persistent scanning for opportunities and connection, distinguished in her framework from multitasking for efficiency. | An attributed conceptual framework. [FAQ](https://lindastone.net/faq/). |
| Email/screen apnea | Stone's description of breath-holding or altered breathing during screen use. The approximately 80% figure in the compilation is attributed to informal observation. | An observational claim, not an established population prevalence or diagnostic rate. [Collected writings](https://lindastone.net/writings/); supplied audit. |
